{
 "esm": "1.3.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "clm_soiltemp",
  "description": "CTSM/CLM snow/soil temperature (stage 2 of the EqESM project): the SoilTemperature model of SoilTemperatureMod.F90 (ctsm5.4.063, cesm3.0-alphabranch checkout, fork commit 1c0d375dd), as the heat-conduction PDE cv*dT/dt = dz*D(K*D(T,lev),lev) + sabg on the column_nonuniform_1d grid, pinned against the W3 stage-1 dump stage1/dumps/clm/clm_soiltemp.csv (LID 261103-111900; column 1, ctype 1 soil, snl = -9, 34 layers, 12 steps; the tests pin column 1 at step 1). The state T is the layer temperature; the SoilThermProp thermal-property laws (F90:604-903) consume the entry state t_entry, as in CLM (SoilThermProp runs at the start of the step): per layer, the snow bulk density bw (:744), the Sturm1997 snow thermal conductivity (:774-778; the traced run's snow_thermal_cond_method; the five coefficients lack _r8 in the Fortran and execute as float32-rounded values, bugs.md #33, reproduced here to rel 1.6e-16), the snow heat capacity with the thin-layer floor (:892-895), the Johansen (1975) soil thermal conductivity (:712-727; saturation water content :712-713, Kersten number :715-719, liquid fraction :720-721, saturated conductivity :722, bedrock override :727), the de Vries (1963) soil heat capacity (:852-854) with the bedrock override (:854), and the harmonic-mean interface conductivity tk with the zero bottom boundary (:825-828). The interface conductivity array K (lev_nodes) is the faq of clm_interface_conductivity over the face index set (K[1] = 0 bottom, K[NLEV+1] = 0 dummy above the top layer). The divergence D(K*D(T,lev),lev) is lowered by the local rule clm_soiltemp_discretization.esm (priority 11, candidate EarthSciDiscretizations PR): interior rows (G[k+1]-G[k])/dz[k], bottom row (G[2]-kdudz_bot)/dz[1], and the top row (kdudz_top - G[NLEV])/M with the capr-weighted measure M = 0.5*(ze[NLEV+1]-zc[NLEV] + capr*(ze[NLEV+1]-zc[NLEV-1])) of F90:1895, kdudz_top = hs + dhsdT*(T[NLEV]-t_entry[NLEV]) the linearized surface flux (ComputeGroundHeatFluxAndDeriv :1545-1798) and kdudz_bot = eflx_bot. The layer index set is the ESD bottom-up column (lev = 26 - j: lev 1 = j = 25 deepest soil, lev 34 = j = -8 top snow; snow j = -8..0, soil j = 1..25). The model is pinned three ways: (1) at the entry state T = t_entry, K, cv, the entry-state interface flux fn_esd = -G (the dumped fn column is exactly -G(t_entry), verified to 1e-13) and the instantaneous dT/dt of the PDE; (2) at the exit state T = t_exit, the instantaneous dT/dt and kdudz_top; (3) the derived Crank-Nicolson identity 0.5*(F(t_entry)+F(t_exit)) = cv*dT/dt (F = dz*D(K*D(u,lev),lev) + sabg), which holds for the interior and bottom rows (lev 1..33) to solver round-off (max |resid| = 6.3e-10 W/m2, computed in Python from the dump before pinning); the top row deviates by the fully-implicit dhsdT term of SetMatrix_Snow and is not pinned (see README.md). The dumped values are reproduced to the dump's full double precision (rel 1e-12). Coverage gaps of the traced dump, each with its reason: imelt = 0 on every row (no phase change in the 12 traced steps), so the Phasechange laws are not exercised; snow_thermal_cond_method = 'Sturm1997' only (the Jordan1991 template exists but is untested); frac_sno_fluxes = 1 exactly; excess_ice = 0 and h2osoi_liq = 0 in the snow layers (the excess-ice and snow-liquid terms never bind); h2osno_no_layers = 0 (the cv(c,1) += cpice*h2osno_no_layers addition of F90:880-882 is not exercised); the top snow layer's absorbed solar (sabg = 57.79 W/m2 in the dump) is inside hs_top_snow (ComputeGroundHeatFluxAndDeriv :1779-1783 adds no sabg to the top row), so the model's sabg parameter carries 0 at the top layer; eflx_bot = 0 in the dump (the sign convention of the F90 comment, +upward, vs the fn slot, +downward, is unpinned; see README.md); the top-layer dumped dz (0.015578352833079012) differs from the grid spacing ze[NLEV+1]-ze[NLEV] (0.015517897173545236), bugs.md #34, so dz stays a dumped parameter.",
  "tags": [
   "land_surface",
   "clm",
   "soil-temperature",
   "heat-conduction",
   "pde",
   "cesm"
  ],
  "created": "2026-11-08T00:00:00Z",
  "authors": [
   "EqESM project contributors"
  ],
  "references": [
   {
    "citation": "Lawrence, D. M., Fisher, R. A., Koven, C. D., Oleson, K. W., Swenson, S. C., Bonan, G., et al. (2019). The Community Land Model Version 5: Description of New Features, Benchmarking, and Impact of Forcing Uncertainty. Journal of Advances in Modeling Earth Systems, 11(12), 4245-4287.",
    "doi": "10.1029/2018MS001583"
   },
   {
    "citation": "CTSM (Community Terrestrial Systems Model), ESCOMP/CTSM, ctsm5.4.063 (cesm3.0-alphabranch): the CLM land-surface source - SoilTemperatureMod.F90 (SoilThermProp, ComputeGroundHeatFluxAndDeriv, ComputeHeatDiffFluxAndFactor, SetRHSVec_Snow, SetRHSVec_Soil, SetMatrix_Snow, SetMatrix_Soil), clm_varcon.F90 (constants) - the reference implementation these components are transcribed from.",
    "url": "https://github.com/ESCOMP/CTSM"
   },
   {
    "citation": "EarthSciModels - the authoritative .esm corpus this component lives in.",
    "url": "https://github.com/EarthSciML/EarthSciModels"
   }
  ],
  "license": "MIT"
 },
 "index_sets": {
  "lev": {
   "kind": "interval",
   "size": "NLEV"
  },
  "lev_nodes": {
   "kind": "interval",
   "size": {
    "op": "+",
    "args": [
     "NLEV",
     1
    ]
   }
  }
 },
 "metaparameters": {
  "NLEV": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 34,
   "description": "number of snow + soil layers of the SoilTemperature column, the column_nonuniform_1d grid's NLEV bound at the import edge (34 in the traced run: 9 snow j = -8..0 plus 25 soil j = 1..25), [-]"
  },
  "N_SNOW_MAX": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 9,
   "description": "number of snow layers of the traced run, |snl| = 9 (the metaparameter replaces the literal 9 of the rejected Crank-Nicolson transcription), [-]"
  },
  "nbedrock": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 20,
   "description": "layer index at which bedrock begins: CLM layers j > nbedrock are bedrock (col%nbedrock; the dump pins nbedrock = 20, i.e. j = 21..25 = ESD lev 1..5; a metaparameter because the bedrock mask is a makearray region bound, which must be compile-time in this ESM dialect), [-]"
  }
 },
 "models": {
  "SoilTemperature": {
   "expression_template_imports": [
    {
     "ref": "./clm_templates.esm"
    },
    {
     "ref": "${ESD_ROOT}/grids/column_nonuniform_1d/grid.esm",
     "bindings": {
      "NLEV": "NLEV"
     }
    },
    {
     "ref": "./clm_soiltemp_discretization.esm",
     "bindings": {
      "NLEV": "NLEV"
     }
    }
   ],
   "expression_templates": {
    "soil_heat_tendency": {
     "description": "Heat-flux divergence of the CLM snow/soil heat-conduction equation, the RHS of cv*dT/dt = F(u): F(u) = dz*D(K*D(u,lev),lev) + sabg, with the divergence lowered by clm_soiltemp_discretization.esm (the capr-weighted top-row measure of SoilTemperatureMod.F90:1895 and the interface fluxes of :825-826; multiplying the lowered divergence by the layer thickness dz reproduces the CLM rows, including the dumped top-layer thickness of bugs.md #34). The operator is linear in the state u with K frozen from the entry state and sabg constant, so it is applied once to the state T (the instantaneous tendency dTdt) and once to the Crank-Nicolson mean state t_avg (the derived identity 0.5*(F(t_entry) + F(t_exit)) = F(t_avg) of the cn_balance test).",
     "params": ["u", "K", "dz", "sabg"],
     "body": {"op": "+", "args": [
      {"op": "*", "args": ["dz", {"op": "D", "args": [
       {"op": "*", "args": ["K", {"op": "D", "args": ["u"], "wrt": "lev"}]}
      ], "wrt": "lev"}]},
      "sabg"
     ]}
    }
   },
   "variables": {
    "ze": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "description": "interface coordinates of the column, ze[n] = -zi_bot(26-n) for n = 1..34 and ze[35] = -zi_top(-8) (dump columns zi_bot/zi_top; the ESD lev axis runs bottom-up so the coordinates are negative downward / positive above the surface), [m]",
     "shape": [
      "lev_nodes"
     ],
     "default": 0.0
    },
    "dz": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "description": "layer thickness dz(j) [m] (dump column dz, exit stage; the top-layer value 0.015578352833079012 differs from the grid spacing ze[NLEV+1]-ze[NLEV], bugs.md #34, so the dumped dz is carried as a parameter and multiplies the lowered divergence)",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "default": 0.0
    },
    "t_entry": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "K",
     "description": "layer temperature at the entry stage, the value SoilThermProp consumes (dump column t_soisno, entry stage; the phase-change flag imelt = 0 on every dumped row)",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "default": 0.0
    },
    "t_exit": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "K",
     "description": "layer temperature at the exit stage, after the band-diagonal solve (dump column t_soisno, exit stage); the exit-pin test sets the state T = t_exit, and the derived CN identity is evaluated between t_entry and t_exit",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "default": 0.0
    },
    "h2osoi_liq": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "kg/m^2",
     "description": "layer liquid water mass (dump column h2osoi_liq, entry stage; 0 in all snow layers of the dump)",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "default": 0.0
    },
    "h2osoi_ice": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "kg/m^2",
     "description": "layer ice mass (dump column h2osoi_ice, entry stage; unchanged entry to exit since imelt = 0 everywhere)",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "default": 0.0
    },
    "excess_ice": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "kg/m^2",
     "description": "excess-ice water equivalent (use_excess_ice = .true. in the run; 0 for all dumped layers), [kg/m2]",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "default": 0.0
    },
    "watsat": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "description": "soil porosity (soil dataset; dump column watsat, entry stage: uniform 0.43482 across j = 1..25; 0.0 dummy for snow layers, sitting in the discarded branch of the layer ifelse)",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "default": 0.0
    },
    "tkmg": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "W/m/K",
     "description": "saturated thermal conductivity of the mineral matrix, tkmg = tkm^(1-watsat) (SoilStateInitTimeConstMod.F90:581; dump column tkmg, entry stage: uniform 3.019245073504738 across j = 1..25; 0.0 dummy for snow layers)",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "default": 0.0
    },
    "tkdry": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "W/m/K",
     "description": "dry soil thermal conductivity (SoilStateInitTimeConstMod.F90:585; dump column tkdry, entry stage: uniform 0.2157223650051119 across j = 1..25; 0.0 dummy for snow layers)",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "default": 0.0
    },
    "csol": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "J/m^3/K",
     "description": "soil matrix volumetric heat capacity (soil dataset; dump column csol, entry stage: uniform 2.20383606557377e6 across j = 1..25; 0.0 dummy for snow layers)",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "default": 0.0
    },
    "sabg": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "description": "solar radiation absorbed in the layer (dump column sabg_lyr_col, exit stage; the NaN soil rows are read as 0). The traced run deposits solar radiation only in lev 30..33 (CLM j = -4..-7); the top snow layer's absorption (57.79 W/m2) is inside hs_top_snow and this parameter carries 0 at the top layer, because SetRHSVec_Snow adds no sabg term to the top row (ComputeGroundHeatFluxAndDeriv :1779-1783), [W/m2]",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "default": 0.0
    },
    "hs": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "description": "surface energy flux at the top of the snowpack, hs_top_snow (dump column hs_top_snow, exit stage; includes the top-layer absorbed solar), [W/m2]",
     "default": 0.0
    },
    "dhsdT": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "W/m^2/K",
     "description": "temperature derivative of the surface energy flux (dump column dhsdT, exit stage), [W/m2/K]",
     "default": 0.0
    },
    "eflx_bot": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "description": "heat flux from beneath the column (dump column eflx_bot, exit stage: 0.0 in the dump; the F90 comment says +upward while the fn slot is +downward, a sign ambiguity unpinned by the zero value, see README.md), [W/m2]",
     "default": 0.0
    },
    "frac_sno_fluxes": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "description": "fraction of the ground covered by snow for heat-flux calculations (waterdiagnosticbulk_inst%frac_sno_fluxes_col; the dump pins 1 exactly)",
     "default": 1.0
    },
    "denh2o": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "kg/m^3",
     "description": "density of liquid water SHR_CONST_RHOFW (clm_varcon.F90:64)",
     "default": 1000.0
    },
    "denice": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "kg/m^3",
     "description": "density of ice SHR_CONST_RHOICE (clm_varcon.F90:65)",
     "default": 917.0
    },
    "cpice": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "J/kg/K",
     "description": "specific heat of ice SHR_CONST_CPICE (clm_varcon.F90:58)",
     "default": 2117.27
    },
    "cpliq": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "J/kg/K",
     "description": "specific heat of liquid water SHR_CONST_CPFW (clm_varcon.F90:57)",
     "default": 4188.0
    },
    "tfrz": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "K",
     "description": "freezing point of water SHR_CONST_TKFRZ (clm_varcon.F90:76)",
     "default": 273.15
    },
    "tkair": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "W/m/K",
     "description": "thermal conductivity of air (clm_varcon.F90:73)",
     "default": 0.023
    },
    "tkice": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "W/m/K",
     "description": "thermal conductivity of ice (clm_varcon.F90:74)",
     "default": 2.29
    },
    "tkwat": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "W/m/K",
     "description": "thermal conductivity of liquid water (clm_varcon.F90:75)",
     "default": 0.57
    },
    "thk_bedrock": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "W/m/K",
     "description": "bedrock thermal conductivity (clm_varcon.F90:121)",
     "default": 3.0
    },
    "csol_bedrock": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "J/m^3/K",
     "description": "bedrock volumetric heat capacity (clm_varcon.F90:123)",
     "default": 2000000.0
    },
    "thin_sfclayer": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "J/m^2/K",
     "description": "heat-capacity floor for thin surface layers, thin_sfclayer = 1.0e-6 (SoilTemperatureMod.F90:85): a J/m2/K floor in the snow heat-capacity law (:892-895), never binding in the dump (every snow layer has cv >> 1e-6)",
     "default": 1e-06
    },
    "capr": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "description": "top snow layer surface-flux weighting capr = 0.34 (clm_varcon.F90:86, SoilTemperatureMod.F90:86), the measure weight of the top-row divergence in clm_soiltemp_discretization.esm, [-]",
     "default": 0.34
    },
    "dt": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "s",
     "description": "land-model time step dtime = 1800 s of the traced run (CLM dt, the dump advances tod by 1800 per step), [s]",
     "default": 1800.0
    },
    "T": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "K",
     "description": "layer temperature state of the heat-conduction PDE cv*dT/dt = dz*D(K*D(T,lev),lev) + sabg, [K]",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ]
    },
    "zc": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m",
     "description": "layer-center coordinates zc[n] = (ze[n] + ze[n+1])/2, the column_nonuniform_1d cell centers (equal to -z(26-n), the dump's z column, exactly), [m]",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ]
    },
    "is_snow": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "description": "snow-layer mask: 1 on lev NLEV-N_SNOW_MAX+1..NLEV (j = -8..0), 0 on the soil layers, [-]",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ]
    },
    "is_bedrock": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "description": "bedrock-layer mask: 1 on lev 1..NLEV-N_SNOW_MAX-nbedrock (j = 21..25), 0 elsewhere, [-]",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ]
    },
    "bw": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "kg/m^3",
     "description": "snow bulk density bw = (h2osoi_ice + h2osoi_liq)/(frac_sno_fluxes*dz), computed on all layers (the soil values sit in the discarded branch of the thk ifelse), [kg/m3]",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ]
    },
    "satw": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "description": "soil water saturation satw = min(1, (h2osoi_liq/denh2o + h2osoi_ice/denice + excess_ice/denice)/(dz*watsat)) (named intermediate of the Johansen law, computed once; soil layers only), [1]",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ]
    },
    "dke": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "description": "Kersten number dke of the Johansen law, dke = satw for frozen soil (t_entry < tfrz, the traced regime) (named intermediate, computed once; soil layers only), [1]",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ]
    },
    "fl": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "description": "liquid fraction of soil water fl (named intermediate of the saturated-conductivity law, computed once; soil layers only), [1]",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ]
    },
    "dksat": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "W/m/K",
     "description": "saturated soil thermal conductivity dksat = tkmg*tkwat^(fl*watsat)*tkice^((1-fl)*watsat) (named intermediate of the Johansen law, computed once; soil layers only), [W/m/K]",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ]
    },
    "thk": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "W/m/K",
     "description": "layer thermal conductivity: Sturm1997 snow conductivity on the snow layers, thk_bedrock on the bedrock layers, Johansen (1975) soil conductivity elsewhere, consuming the entry state t_entry (SoilThermProp runs at the step start), [W/m/K]",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ]
    },
    "cv": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "J/m^2/K",
     "description": "layer heat capacity per unit ground area: snow_heat_capacity with the thin-layer floor on the snow layers, csol_bedrock*dz on the bedrock layers, de Vries (1963) soil heat capacity elsewhere, [J/m2/K]",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ]
    },
    "K": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "W/m/K",
     "description": "interface thermal conductivity on the face axis: K[n] = clm_interface_conductivity(thk[n-1], thk[n], zc[n-1], zc[n], ze[n]) for n = 2..NLEV (the harmonic mean of SoilTemperatureMod.F90:825-826), K[1] = 0 (no interface below the bottom layer, :828), K[NLEV+1] = 0 dummy (no interface above the top snow layer; the surface flux enters through kdudz_top instead), [W/m/K]",
     "shape": [
      "lev_nodes"
     ]
    },
    "kdudz_top": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "description": "surface diffusive flux K du/dz on the top interface, linearized as hs + dhsdT*(T[NLEV] - t_entry[NLEV]) about the entry state (the top-row flux of SetMatrix_Snow), [W/m2]",
     "default": 0.0
    },
    "kdudz_bot": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "description": "bottom diffusive flux K du/dz on the surface interface (lev 1), the prescribed eflx_bot of the bottom row, [W/m2]",
     "default": 0.0
    },
    "fn_esd": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "description": "heat diffusion through the interface below layer n, fn_esd[n] = -G[n] = -interface_flux_K_lev(T, K, n) for n = 2..NLEV and fn_esd[1] = kdudz_bot (the dump column fn is exactly -G(t_entry), verified to 1e-13), [W/m2]",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ]
    },
    "dTdt": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "K/s",
     "description": "instantaneous layer temperature tendency of the PDE, dTdt = (dz*D(K*D(T,lev),lev) + sabg)/cv, the RHS evaluated at the current state, [K/s]",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ]
    },
    "t_avg": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "K",
     "description": "arithmetic mean of the entry and exit states, t_avg = 0.5*(t_entry + t_exit); because the flux operator is linear in the state (K frozen from t_entry, sabg constant), 0.5*(F(t_entry) + F(t_exit)) = dz*D(K*D(t_avg,lev),lev) + sabg, the Crank-Nicolson average of the dumped step, [K]",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ]
    },
    "cn_balance": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "description": "derived Crank-Nicolson energy-balance residual cn_balance = 0.5*(F(t_entry) + F(t_exit)) - cv*(t_exit - t_entry)/dt with F(u) = dz*D(K*D(u,lev),lev) + sabg; with the dumped entry/exit states it evaluates to the CLM solver's round-off on the interior and bottom rows (max |resid| = 6.3e-10 W/m2, computed in Python before pinning), pinning that t_exit solves the CLM tridiagonal system. The top row deviates by the fully-implicit dhsdT term of SetMatrix_Snow (see README.md) and is not pinned, [W/m2]",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ]
    }
   },
   "equations": [
    {
     "lhs": "zc",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "apply_expression_template",
      "args": [],
      "name": "column_cell_center",
      "bindings": {
       "ze": "ze"
      }
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "is_snow",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "makearray",
      "args": [],
      "regions": [
       [
        [
         1,
         {
          "op": "-",
          "args": [
           "NLEV",
           "N_SNOW_MAX"
          ]
         }
        ]
       ],
       [
        [
         {
          "op": "+",
          "args": [
           {
            "op": "-",
            "args": [
             "NLEV",
             "N_SNOW_MAX"
            ]
           },
           1
          ]
         },
         "NLEV"
        ]
       ]
      ],
      "values": [
